# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile is this directory (platform/).
#
# Two jobs: keep the context small, and make it impossible for a secret or a
# host-built artefact to be baked into an image.

# ── never, under any circumstances ───────────────────────────────────────────
# A .env in the context is one `COPY . .` away from a JWT secret in a published
# image layer. .env.example carries names and no values, and the image has no
# use for it either.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ── host artefacts: the image builds its own ─────────────────────────────────
# A host node_modules is the wrong platform's binaries (bcrypt and the Prisma
# engines are native) and would silently shadow the install done in the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── test and tooling output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.log
**/.eslintcache

# ── repository and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# ── not part of the API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Postgres only; the deployed database is Supabase.
docker-compose.yml
**/*.md
